 "meaning": "A well-known simile closes the round of salutations: whatever god has been greeted — Sandhyā, the directions, Yama, Hari-Hara, the Sun — the homage travels on, as rain falling anywhere ends in the ocean, to Keśava. The last words are repeated with om namaḥ iti, and the worshipper then says the abhivādana again.",
 "in_the_rite": "Step sūrya-nārāyaṇa-vandana, all three services, the last of its four verses, followed by the abhivādana.",
